// A fragment entry's `out` parameter with NO SEMANTIC binds to COLOR
// (t_a15ec129).
//
// The store was gated on the parameter HAVING a semantic, so this shader
// emitted no StoreOutput at all - and then everything that only fed the
// output went with it.  diffuse_specular came out as eleven instructions,
// none of them writing the output register, with an input mask naming
// three varyings the ucode never read: exit 0, no diagnostic, four corpus
// rows mismatching for two days.
//
// The reference defaults it.  Its parameter table for a shader declared
// this way reads "out.UNDEFINED: COLOR0" - declared semantic undefined,
// resource COLOR0.
//
// Its twin fp_out_with_semantic_f.cg is the same shader with `: COLOR`
// written out.  The test requires the two to compile to the same PROGRAM -
// identical ucode - which is the whole claim: the semantic is not optional
// information, it is information the compiler already has.  Not the same
// CONTAINER: the reference records the declared semantic beside the
// resource, "out.UNDEFINED: COLOR0" here against "out.COLOR: COLOR0"
// there, and ours matches each of those byte for byte.
void main(float4 color : TEXCOORD0,
          out float4 oColor)
{
    oColor = color;
}
